{
  "name": "Schedule posts from a Google Sheets content calendar with Socialync",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nEvery hour this workflow takes the first row marked Ready in a Google Sheets content calendar and schedules it with Socialync. The row gives the caption, the platforms, an optional image or video link and the time. The workflow first sets the row to Scheduling, so no later run can take it again. The sheet then shows the result in Status and Notes: Scheduled with the post ID, or Needs fixing with the reason. A row with a problem never stops the next row from running on the next hour.\n\nPosts are scheduled without a manual approval step. You can cancel or change any scheduled post in Socialync until it goes out.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create an API key at https://socialync.io/go/n8n-node-keys and add it as a Socialync credential.\n2. Add a Google Sheets credential.\n3. Make a sheet with these columns: Caption, Platforms, Publish at, Image URL, Video URL, Title, Status, Notes. Type times as 2026-11-12 09:30 in a plain text column. Set Status to Ready.\n4. Choose the sheet in all five Google Sheets nodes. Set your time zone in Settings.\n5. Connect your platforms in Socialync first.\n\n### Customization\nLeave Platforms empty to use the list in Settings. Instagram needs an image or a video. YouTube needs a Title. TikTok needs a privacy level in Settings.\n\nA row stuck on Scheduling means a run stopped part way. Check Socialync, then set the row to Scheduled or Ready.\n\nAPI reference: https://socialync.io/go/n8n-node",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 600
      },
      "id": "c3621d01-7391-456a-a4d5-d7bc0b41b2de",
